###### [Carmichael numbers](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carmichael_number) 
A *Carmichael number* will *usually* pass *Fermat primality test* even though it is *not* actually prime. But this test $isPrime$ is searching divisors *exhausively*, so its perfect but *not* efficient. So $isPrime$ *cannot* be fooled by the first 16 Carmichael numbers.

